n mostly non-operating.", "authority": "SEC C&DI 103.01, 103.02"}, {"rule": "Free cash flow is operating cash flow less capital expenditures, and the definition is stated beside the number because it has no uniform one.", "authority": "SEC C&DI 102.07"}, {"rule": "Credit measures built on interest (coverage, leverage) are refused for a financial issuer: interest is a bank's operating cost and deposits its raw material. ROE, ROA and the accruals ratio do apply to banks.", "authority": "the formula registry's not_for_financials"}, {"rule": "Segment, product, geographic and customer-concentration figures are not held as facts; they are quoted from the filing's own sentences, cited, never derived from parts.", "authority": "ASC 280; Regulation S-K Item 101(c)"}, {"rule": "A name the desk has not prepared is started (readiness) and said to be in preparation; nothing is estimated for it meanwhile.", "authority": "the desk's readiness pipeline"}], "next": ["describe('MSFT', expand='<domain>')", "run: {\"fn\": \"fundamentals\", \"ticker\": \"MSFT\", \"metric\": \"<line>\"}", "read_filings('MSFT', item='1A')", "run: {\"fn\": \"prices\", \"ticker\": \"MSFT\", \"window\": \"1y\"}"], "catalogue_as_of": "2026-09-13", "how_to_read": "Every listed name carries `is` (what it is) and `call` (how to read or compute it); a domain carries `open`. `methods` are what compute produces for this subject. `procedures` are the analyst's domains for this kind of subject, each with its question, the words it is asked in, its methods and what it reads \u2014 open one with expand=<domain>. `methods_that_refuse_here` are that domain's methods this subject's own filings cannot feed, with why: do not spend a call on them. `desk_rules` are this desk's own conventions; `not_held` and `cannot` are figures this desk does not have and why \u2014 say so, do not substitute. `next` lists the calls that open the next level.", "withheld": "Some measures this run computed are withheld pending validation and ar